<attribute name="refinedDescription" nodeId="690e1f19">&lt;p&gt;
    A security design may include the following:
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Design of authentication security model, authorization controls and security reporting
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Guiding principles and authentication standards
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Role design and definitions
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Authentication security model, authorization controls and security reporting across multiple environments
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Logical access paths
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Authentication points
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Entitlements
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Controls
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Global package settings and administrator rights
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Authentication management process
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        User access rights, roles and responsibilities&lt;br /&gt;
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;</attribute>
</Element>
